  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 240 AM CDT Fri Apr 17 2026\n\nTemperatures will plummet behind the cold front. Low temperatures \nwill be below freezing in the northern half of the state by Saturday \nmorning. Breezy northwest winds statewide will bring wind chills \ninto the 20s. Highs Saturday will recover into the 50s. 60s start to \nreturn Sunday.\n\nUpper-level ridging over the Rockies will bring a relatively dry \nperiod with sustained warming early next week. Behind it will be \nanother region of troughing, perhaps containing a closed low. Broad \nPoPs exist Wednesday and beyond, covering shower and storm potential \nfor when this feature eventually influences weather across the \nPlains.",
